Your new issue is ready to print!

<%= @issue.title %> is waiting to help you beat the scroll. Print it, staple it, and read the good bits away from the screen.

Print your issue:
<%= @issue_url %>

<% if @featured_articles.any? %>
A few pieces waiting inside:
<% if @featured_authors.any? %>
Featuring <%= @featured_authors.to_sentence %>.
<% end %>

<% @featured_articles.each do |article| %>
<% metadata = [article["source"], article["author"].presence && "by #{article['author']}"].compact.join(" / ") %>
- <%= article["title"] %><%= " (#{metadata})" if metadata.present? %>
<% end %>

<% end %>
<% if @articles.any? %>
Issue stats:
- <%= @articles.size %> articles
- <%= @stats.reading_minutes %> minute read
- <%= @stats.source_count %> sources
- <%= @stats.scroll_meters %>m of scroll avoided

<% end %>
Print instructions:

1. Open the issue and press the Print button.
2. Set your printer to double-sided printing and set flip on short edge.
3. Fold the stack in half and staple the spine.
4. Take it somewhere quiet and enjoy.
